## Disagreements with the reviews (not applied as written)
1. a#1 — the reviewer claims the English says "advertisement" and asks for "việc đăng quảng cáo". The English
   source (src/lib/llms-txt.ts L122) says "guaranteed visibility", so I wrote "việc bảo đảm được hiển thị" and
   applied the rest of the row ("thứ hạng trên công cụ tìm kiếm", "sự bảo trợ", "trí tuệ nhân tạo").
2. a#18 — "Menu" cannot be used; guidance-chrome-language.test.ts asserts menuLabel !== 'Menu' (it is the exact
   English fallback the test guards against). Used "Trình đơn".
3. a#38 — reviewer's "Luật Khuyến khích Đổi mới Công nghiệp" adds "Khuyến khích" (promotion), which 產業創新條例
   does not say. Used "Luật Đổi mới Công nghiệp".
4. a#43 — the reviewer asks to delete the parenthetical joke in 006. Blocks may not be added or removed, so the
   block was rewritten neutrally instead of deleted.
5. a#52 — see skip note (the English source keeps the Difficulty row).
6. b#3 — reviewer suggested "đăng ký cư trú"; ACCEPTED-vi prescribes "đăng ký hộ khẩu (戶籍)", which is what I used.
7. b#6 — reviewer's "kế toán sư" is not Vietnamese usage; ACCEPTED-vi's "kế toán viên công chứng (會計師, CPA)" used.
8. b#33 — "Liên hệ (không tư vấn bằng tiếng Việt)" reads as a negative label in a related-links list. ACCEPTED-vi
   allows rewording a relabelled link, so the label is plain "Liên hệ" (the pack's own nav word); the consultation
   -language lock is stated on the target page and in the guidance/FAQ strings, and nothing implies vi consultation.
9. b#44 — reviewer's "Vụ Thương mại" adopted, but glossed 商業發展署 (the agency's current name, already used in 001)
   rather than 商業司, and 001 was aligned to the same Vietnamese name so the locale has exactly one.

